  {
    "_ulid": "01KJDQ173NEFK9RFZGRS22VG6M",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Shadow branch index inconsistency: observation @01KJ73ME appeared in search results but failed on ks",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: `kspec search` can find observations (e.g., @01KJ73ME) via `loadMetaContext()` which reads the meta.observations array from kynetic.yaml, but `kspec item get` fails for the same reference because the `ReferenceIndex` only indexes spec items and tasks — not meta entities like observations, workflows, conventions, or agents.\n\nThis is not a write conflict or index corruption. It is an architectural gap: search and item-get use different resolution paths. Search loads observations from meta context, while item-get only resolves through the ReferenceIndex which does not include meta entities.\n\n**Where**:\n- `src/cli/commands/search.ts` — loads observations via `loadMetaContext()` (lines 241-257)\n- `src/cli/commands/item.ts` — uses `refIndex.resolve()` which only covers spec items\n- `src/parser/refs.ts` — `ReferenceIndex` class that builds the resolution index\n- `src/cli/commands/meta.ts` — has dedicated `meta observe get` subcommand for observations\n\n**How**:\nTwo options (pick one):\n1. **Extend ReferenceIndex** to include meta entities (observations, workflows, agents, conventions) so `item get` can resolve them. This is the deeper fix but has namespace collision risk.\n2. **Improve error message** in `item get` to suggest `kspec meta observe get @ref` when a ref fails to resolve, since observations have their own dedicated get command. This is lighter and avoids mixing namespaces.\n\nOption 2 is recommended: observations already have `kspec meta observe get`, so the real bug is a confusing UX, not missing functionality.\n\n**Done when**:\n- `kspec item get @observation-ref` either resolves the observation or provides a clear error message suggesting `kspec meta observe get @ref`\n- Alternatively, if extending ReferenceIndex: meta entities are resolvable via `item get` with correct type display",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "status": "pending",
