    "title": "CLI args should accept both kebab-case and underscore variants (e.g. depends-on and depends_on). Cur",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: Batch command validation rejects underscore variants of argument names (e.g., `depends_on`) even though kebab-case (`depends-on`) and camelCase (`dependsOn`) are accepted. Agents generating JSON batch payloads naturally use underscores, which is the standard JSON/Python naming convention. The error message suggests the kebab form, creating a frustrating feedback loop.\n\n**Where**:\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 180-216 — `kebabToCamel()` and `getKnownArgNames()` functions\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 308-327 — unknown arg validation loop\n- `src/cli/batch-exec.ts` lines 434-496 — `buildCommandArgv()` which also needs to handle underscore keys when building CLI argv\n\n**How**:\n1. Add a `underscoreToKebab()` or `underscoreToCamel()` normalizer alongside `kebabToCamel()`.\n2. In `getKnownArgNames()`, add underscore variants to the known names set (e.g., for `depends-on`, also add `depends_on`).\n3. In `buildCommandArgv()`, normalize incoming arg keys before classification — convert underscores to kebab-case before looking up in positionalNameSet and optionMap.\n4. In the required-args check (lines 330-348), also check underscore variants.\n\nA cleaner approach: add a single `normalizeArgKey(key)` function that converts any variant (kebab, camel, underscore) to a canonical form, then use it everywhere.\n\n**Done when**:\n- `{\"command\": \"task set\", \"args\": {\"ref\": \"@task\", \"depends_on\": [\"@dep1\"]}}` works in batch mode\n- All three forms accepted: `depends-on`, `dependsOn`, `depends_on`\n- Same normalization applies to all options, not just depends_on\n- Add test cases for underscore variant args in batch validation tests",
